# Brunnwinkl village house wall as a SOLID block (the Kornmuehle, houses 2-5):
# whitewash w with a green G shuttered window (m frame, b glass, s glint) and
# an i stucco sill per tile. Exposed top = a timber upper storey (o lip,
# O boards with l joints every 4 px, l shadow) over whitewash without window;
# exposed left i, right i/m, bottom = i/m/d plinth: the light top lip and dark
# edges set it apart from St. Gilgen's flat decorative wall_village_bg (art-style 8).
# Autotiled (D-020): anim `auto`, frame = neighbour mask
# (1 = same tile above, 2 = right, 4 = below, 8 = left; level edge = same).
# Drawn by the pixel-artist with a throwaway script; the grids below are the source.
sprite = tile_facade_village
size   = 16x16
origin = 0,0
anim   = auto frames=16 ticks=1
